### 🟡 Minor (recommended)
- `evals/orchestration/tasks/t14-constraint-horizon/oracle.sh:5` — The added comment states "runner passes it as $1 — same contract as the other oracles," but this is **false for every current caller**. Verified by full-repo grep (`oracle\.sh\b`) across the codebase: the only two invocation sites are `evals/orchestration/run-orchestration-eval.sh:306-311` (`cp "$TASK_DIR/oracle.sh" "$TEMP_REPO/oracle.sh"; cd "$TEMP_REPO"; bash oracle.sh` — zero args) and `hooks/tests/orchestration-eval.test.sh` (every T1–T8 block, e.g. lines 29/63/86/111/…/395, calls `bash oracle.sh` with no argument, cwd already set to the candidate copy). Because of this, the added `if [ $# -ge 1 ]; then cd "$1"; fi` (lines 6-8) is **dead code under every existing call site** — it never fires. This isn't a new regression (`t10-t13-log-parser/oracle.sh:6-8` etc. already carry the identical inert guard, just without a comment), but the *new comment* asserts a concrete, checkable fact about the harness contract that the harness itself contradicts. Impact: a future engineer editing `run-orchestration-eval.sh` or authoring `t15`+ oracles may trust this comment and design around a `$1`-passing contract that doesn't exist, or wrongly assume t14 is exercised with an explicit repo-path argument. Fix: either correct the comment ("currently unused — oracle.sh is always invoked via `bash oracle.sh` with cwd already the candidate repo per `run-orchestration-eval.sh:306-311`; this guard is defensive, matching the t10-t13 convention, not a live contract") or drop the block since it does nothing today.

### 🔵 Suggestion (consider)
- `evals/orchestration/tasks/t14-constraint-horizon/oracle.sh` (whole file, pre-existing gap not introduced by this diff) — `hooks/tests/orchestration-eval.test.sh` only exercises T1–T8 (verified: grepping that file for `t9-|t10-|t11-|t12-|t13-|t14-` returns zero matches). T14's oracle logic — and this diff's own change to it — has **no automated pristine-fails/fixed-passes check**, unlike every task T1-T8. Impact: the misleading comment above (and any future regression in this oracle) would go undetected by the test suite. Fix: add a T14 block to `hooks/tests/orchestration-eval.test.sh` mirroring the T1-T8 pattern; this would also have forced verification of the actual invocation contract before the comment was written.
- Bundling concern: the mode-bit changes to `scripts/error-path-scan.sh` / `scripts/secret-scan-diff.js` are functionally unrelated to the t14 `oracle.sh` cd/comment change (different subsystem, different concern). Both fixes are individually legitimate (see Verified Clean), but combining unrelated fixes in one diff reduces `git blame`/bisect precision. Without the original commit message I can't rule this in or out as a真正 scope violation — flagging for the author/dispatcher to confirm both were part of one stated task.

